"The patient, a 72-year-old male with a PSA of 4.5 and a clinical T-stage of cT1c based on digital rectal examination, presents with a predicted recurrence-free survival of 330 months. This long-term prediction is based on the established prognostic factors derived from the Cox model. Further clinical follow-up is required to monitor actual recurrence rates and assess the reliability of this long-term projection."